-- title:
--   Full Slice Commutation Q SDDOp Avg Eq
-- statement:
--   **The averaged full-slice operator distance equals twice the quartic commutation gap.**
--
--   Let $(q,m,d)$ have a field model, let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the successor space, and let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family. Form the two raw operator families by applying `fullSliceProductLeft` and `fullSliceProductRight` to the full-slice question associated with each uniformly sampled evaluated-slice question. Their averaged state-dependent squared-distance error is exactly twice the difference between the full-slice $ABA$ and $\mathrm{ABAB}$ scalar averages:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{sddErrorOp}_S(\mathcal U,\mathrm{fullSliceProductLeft},\mathrm{fullSliceProductRight})
--   =2\left(\mathrm{fullSliceABAAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})
--   -\mathrm{fullSliceABABAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})\right).
--   $$
--
--   The identity is an exact algebraic expansion, with no normalization or error hypothesis. It converts the operator-distance formulation of full-slice commutation into the scalar quartic gap used by the downstream evaluated-slice theorem.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.fullSliceCommutation_qSDDOp_avg_eq`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/Transport/FullSlice/Bridges/QSDD.lean#L120-L180

